{
 "fps": 30,
 "totalFrames": 1735,
 "lines": [
  {
   "i": 0,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You just bought a shiny new razor for ten dollars. What a bargain.",
   "from": 0,
   "to": 102
  },
  {
   "i": 1,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "First shave? Smooth as a dolphin. You feel like a movie star.",
   "from": 106,
   "to": 210
  },
  {
   "i": 2,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Two weeks later, the blade tugs your face like tiny pliers.",
   "from": 214,
   "to": 302
  },
  {
   "i": 3,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "You go buy refills, and they're locked in a glass case.",
   "from": 306,
   "to": 384
  },
  {
   "i": 4,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Right next to the perfume, the phones and the fancy watches.",
   "from": 387,
   "to": 465
  },
  {
   "i": 5,
   "speaker": "clerk",
   "text": "Eight refills? That comes to forty dollars.",
   "from": 469,
   "to": 575
  },
  {
   "i": 6,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Four times the price of the razor. The handle was just the bait.",
   "from": 594,
   "to": 694
  },
  {
   "i": 7,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Inside each refill, the steel costs well under five cents.",
   "from": 698,
   "to": 790
  },
  {
   "i": 8,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "The plastic adds another three to five cents.",
   "from": 794,
   "to": 865
  },
  {
   "i": 9,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "All the materials? Under thirty cents. The shelf price? Five dollars.",
   "from": 868,
   "to": 993
  },
  {
   "i": 10,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "That's fifteen to twenty times what the stuff is worth.",
   "from": 997,
   "to": 1067
  },
  {
   "i": 11,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "In nineteen oh-four, a razor maker patented the throwaway blade.",
   "from": 1070,
   "to": 1174
  },
  {
   "i": 12,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Sell the handle once. Sell the blades forever.",
   "from": 1178,
   "to": 1252
  },
  {
   "i": 13,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "And to keep you paying, they keep adding blades.",
   "from": 1256,
   "to": 1328
  },
  {
   "i": 14,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Two blades in the early seventies. Seven blades by twenty seventeen.",
   "from": 1331,
   "to": 1426
  },
  {
   "i": 15,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "At this rate, your next razor comes with a tiny lawnmower.",
   "from": 1430,
   "to": 1519
  },
  {
   "i": 16,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "No wonder the store guards them like diamonds.",
   "from": 1523,
   "to": 1590
  },
  {
   "i": 17,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "Back at the shelf, a new guy grabs a shiny ten dollar razor.",
   "from": 1593,
   "to": 1679
  },
  {
   "i": 18,
   "speaker": "narrator",
   "text": "What a bargain.",
   "from": 1683,
   "to": 1711
  }
 ],
